\v 1 \add ≈Once\add* the¦224338 wall¦224338 had¦224337 been¦224337 rebuilt¦224337 and¦224339 the¦224340 doors¦224340 \add ≈hung\add* in the gates, the¦224342 gatekeepers¦224342 and¦224343 the¦224343 singers¦224343 and¦224344 the¦224344 Levites¦224344 had¦224341 been¦224341 appointed¦224341.
\v 2 I¦224346 put my¦224350 brother¦224350 Hanani¦224349 and¦224351 the¦224354 fortress¦224355 commander¦224354 Hananyah¦224353 in charge¦224346 over¦224356 Yerushalem¦224358. (\add @Hananyah¦224361\add* was¦224362 a¦224362 \add ≈faithful¦224363\add* man¦224362 and¦224364 \add ≈respected¦224364\add* God more¦224368 than¦224368 many¦224368 \add others do\add*.)
\v 3 I¦224370 told¦224370 them¦224372, “Don't¦224373 open¦224374 Yerushalem's¦224376 gates¦224375 until¦224377 \add ≈broad daylight\add*, and¦224381 then shut¦224384 and¦224386 bar them¦224386 again while \add ≈the¦224388 guards¦224388 are still on full alert\add*. And \add ≈assign¦224387 neighbourhood watch groups among the¦224389 inhabitants¦224389 to keep an eye on their own areas\add*.”
