\v 73 \add ≈So¦225128\add* the¦225129 priests¦225129 and¦225130 the¦225130 Levites¦225130, the¦225131 gatekeepers¦225131 and¦225132 the¦225132 singers¦225132, the¦225136 temple¦225136 workers and¦225141 the rest of the Israelis¦225145, all¦225137 \add ≈settled\add* in¦225146 their \add various ancestral\add* cities.\x + \xo 7:73: \xt 1Ch 9:2; Neh 11:3.\x*
\c 8
\s1 Ezra reads God's instructions to the people
\rem /s1 Ezra Reads the Law to the People
\p
\v 1 All¦225149 the¦225151 people¦225151 gathered¦225148 \add ≈together in¦225158 the¦225159 plaza near\add* the¦225161 Water¦225161 Gate¦225159 and¦225162 \add ≈asked¦225162\add* Ezra¦225163 the¦225164 scribe¦225164 to¦225165 bring¦225165 the¦225168 scroll¦225168 with \add ≈Yahweh's¦225174 instructions¦225173 to Yisrael¦225177 given through\add* Mosheh¦225170 \add !(Moses¦225170)\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈So it was the beginning of October when\add* Ezra¦225180 the¦225181 priest¦225181 brought¦225179 the¦225184 \add ≈scroll\add* to¦225185 the¦225185 gathering¦225186 of¦225185 \add #men¦225187\add* and¦225188 \add #women¦225190\add* and¦225191 everyone who¦225192 wanted to¦225193 understand¦225192 it,
\v 3 and¦225199 he¦225199 \add ≈read it¦225201 aloud in¦225202 the plaza near\add* the Water¦225209 Gate¦225207—reading from¦225210 dawn until¦225213 the¦225215 middle¦225215 of¦225215 the¦225216 day¦225216 in¦225217 front¦225217 of¦225217 those¦225220 men¦225218 and¦225219 women¦225219 and¦225220 \add ≈interested people¦225224, who¦225220 all¦225222 listened intently\add*.
\p
\v 4 Ezra¦225231 the¦225232 scribe¦225232 stood¦225230 on¦225233 a¦225235 raised wooden¦225237 platform¦225235 that¦225238 they had¦225239 made¦225239 \add ≈especially for this purpose\add*. Standing¦225241 on his¦225251 right¦225251 were Mattitiah¦225243, Shema¦225244, Anayah¦225245, Uriyah¦225246, Hilkiyah¦225247, and Ma'aseyah, and on¦225249 his¦225252 left¦225252 \add ≡stood¦225230\add* Pedayah¦225253, Misha'el, Malkiyah¦225255, Hashum¦225256, Hashbaddanah¦225257, Zekaryah¦225258, and Meshullam¦225259.
\p
\v 5 \add ≈Up on the platform,\add* Ezra¦225263 opened¦225262 the¦225264 \add ≈scroll¦225264 in front\add* of all the people, and¦225276 \add ≈as¦225276 he¦225276 did so\add*, all¦225278 the¦225280 people¦225280 stood¦225277 up¦225277.
\v 6 Ezra¦225283 blessed¦225282 the¦225288 great¦225288 God Yahweh and¦225289 the¦225292 people¦225292 \add ≈raised¦225296 their¦225297 arms¦225297 and¦225298 responded¦225289\add*, “May it be so.” Then they¦225298 knelt down¦225299 and¦225299 bowed¦225299 to¦225300 Yahweh¦225300 \add ≈with their faces¦225301\add* to¦225302 the¦225302 ground¦225302.
\p
\v 7 Then¦225304 Yeshua¦225304, Bani¦225305, Shereveyah¦225306, Yamin¦225310, Akkub¦225311, Shabtai, Hodiyyah¦225314, Ma'aseyah, Kelita¦225316, Azaryah¦225317, Yozavad¦225318, Hanan¦225319, Pelayah¦225320, who were all Levites¦225321, \add ≈explained what had been¦225322 read\add* to the people standing there.
\v 8 They¦225332 read¦225332 the scroll¦225333 containing God's instructions¦225334, \add ≈explaining how it applied so¦225337\add* the¦225338 people could understand¦225339 \add *it\add*.
\p
\v 9 Then¦225343 Nehemyah¦225344 the¦225346 governor¦225346 and¦225347 Ezra¦225347 the¦225348 priest¦225348 & scribe¦225350, and¦225351 the¦225351 Levites¦225351 who¦225352 were¦225352 \add ≈explaining it\add*, said¦225343 to¦225356 all¦225356 the¦225358 people¦225358, “Today is¦225360 a sacred¦225360 day¦225359—it¦225362 belongs to¦225363 your¦225364 god¦225364 Yahweh¦225363. Don't¦225365 mourn¦225367 or weep¦225370.” \add That was\add* because¦225371 all¦225373 the¦225375 people¦225375 were¦225372 weeping¦225372 after they¦225376 heard¦225376 \add ≈Yahweh's instructions¦225380 to them\add*.
\v 10 Then¦225382 \add @Nehemyah¦225382\add* told¦225382 them¦225383, “Go¦225384 \add home and\add* eat¦225385 \add ≈some special food¦225386 with sweet¦225388 drink¦225387\add*, and¦225389 \add ≈share some with\add* those \add ≈who can't¦225391 afford such things¦225388\add* because¦225394 today is¦225396 \add ≈a sacred¦225396 day¦225397 that\add* belongs to¦225398 our¦225398 master¦225398. And¦225399 don't¦225399 grieve¦225401, because¦225402 \add ≈the¦225404 happiness from Yahweh¦225405 will make you all strong\add*.”
\p
\v 11 The¦225409 Levites¦225409 \add ≈told the¦225413 people¦225413 to¦225414 quieten down\add*, saying¦225414, “\add ≈Don't¦225419 grieve¦225421 today because¦225416 it's a sacred¦225418 day¦225417. Stay quiet¦225410.\add*”
\v 12 \add ≈So¦225423\add* all¦225424 the¦225426 people¦225426 went¦225423 to¦225427 eat¦225427 and¦225428 drink¦225428 and¦225429 to \add ≈take plates of food to others\add*, and¦225431 to¦225431 \add ≈have a big¦225433 celebration\add* because¦225434 they¦225435 understood¦225435 what \add ≈had¦225438 been read\add* to¦225439 them¦225439.
\s1 The celebration in shelters
\rem /s1 The Festival of Shelters; The Festival of Booths Celebrated
\p
\v 13 The \add ≈next\add* day¦225442, \add ≈all¦225447 the¦225449 clan leaders\add*, and the¦225450 priests¦225450 and¦225451 Levites¦225451, met¦225444 with Ezra¦225454 the¦225455 scribe¦225455 to¦225456 \add ≈study¦225456 the instructions¦225460\add* \add on the scroll\add*.
\v 14 They¦225462 \add ≈discovered¦225462 that it was\add* written¦225463 in¦225464 the \add ≈instructions¦225464 that¦225465 Yahweh¦225467 had¦225466 given through¦225468 Mosheh¦225470\add*, that¦225471 the¦225473 Israelis¦225475 should live¦225472 in¦225476 \add temporary\add* shelters during the celebration¦225477 in¦225478 \add &their¦225479\add* seventh¦225479 month¦225478 \add (our September-October)\add*.\x + \xo 8:14-15: \xt Lev 23:33-36,39-43; Deu 16:13-15.\x*
\v 15 They¦225482 should \add ≈publicly proclaim¦225482\add* in¦225488 Yerushalem¦225488 and¦225483 in¦225485 all¦225485 their¦225487 towns¦225487 \add ≈that¦225481 the people should go¦225490 into the¦225491 hills¦225491 and¦225492 bring¦225492 back branches from olive or wild olive trees¦225498, myrtle¦225501 or palm¦225503 trees¦225503, and¦225504/or other\add* leafy¦225506 trees to¦225507 make¦225507 shelters as it's written¦225509.
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦225512\add* the¦225513 people¦225513 went¦225512 out¦225512 and¦225514 brought¦225514 \add back branches\add* to make¦225515 shelters for¦225516 themselves on¦225519 their \add #roofs¦225521\add* or in¦225522 their courtyards, or in¦225523 the¦225523 temple¦225524 courtyard¦225523 or in¦225526 the¦225526 plazas near the¦225527 Water¦225528 Gate¦225527 and¦225529 the Efrayim¦225531 Gate.
\v 17 Then¦225533 the¦225536 whole¦225534 assembly¦225536 \add ≈of¦225551 people¦225555\add* who'd come back from¦225538 captivity¦225540 made¦225533 shelters and¦225543 lived¦225543 in¦225544 them \add for one week\add*. The¦225551 \add ≈Israelis¦225556\add* hadn't done¦225548 that¦225559 since¦225549 the¦225549 \add ≈time¦225549 of¦225549 Yehoshua's leadership\add*, and¦225560 \add ≈they did it¦225560 with a lot of celebration\add*.
\v 18 \add @Ezra¦225565\add* read aloud from the¦225566 scroll¦225566 of¦225566 God's instructions¦225567 each day of the seven¦225582 days¦225583 of celebration, then¦225584 on¦225584 the¦225585 eighth¦225585 day they all gathered¦225586 together as per the¦225587 instructions.
\c 9
\s1 The people confess their sins
\rem /s1 The People Confess Their Sins; National Confession; The Israelites Confess Their Sins
\p
\v 1 On¦225590 the 24th of that¦225594 month¦225593, the¦225596 \add ≈Israelis¦225598 dressed in¦225600 sackcloth¦225600, put dust on their heads, fasted¦225599, and gathered¦225595 together\add*.
\v 2 Those of¦225605 \add ≈Jewish descent stood¦225610 separately¦225604\add* from¦225607 the descendants¦225608 of¦225608 \add ≈foreigners¦225609\add*, and¦225611 they¦225611 confessed¦225611 their \add own\add* sins¦225614, as well as those of their¦225616 ancestors¦225616.
\v 3 They¦225618 stood¦225618 and¦225622 \add ≈listened to the¦225623 scroll¦225623 with Yahweh's¦225625 instructions¦225624 being read¦225622 for three hours\add*, then¦225629 for \add ≈another three hours\add* they¦225630 confessed¦225630 and¦225631 bowed¦225631 down¦225631 to¦225632 Yahweh¦225632 their god.
\v 4 Then¦225636 Yeshua¦225641 went up¦225636 the Levites'¦225640 stairs with Bani¦225642, Kadmi'el, Shevanyah¦225644, Bunni¦225645, Shereveyah¦225646, \add another\add* Bani¦225647, \add and\add* Kenani¦225648, and¦225649 they¦225649 called¦225649 out¦225649 loudly to¦225652 their¦225655 god¦225655 Yahweh¦225654.
\p
\v 5 Then¦225657 \add ≈some\add* Levites¦225658 (Yeshua¦225659, Kadmi'el, Bani¦225661, Hashavneyah¦225662, Shereveyah¦225663, Hodiyyah¦225664, Shevanyah¦225665, and Petahyah¦225666) said¦225657, “\add ≈Stand\add* up \add and\add* bless¦225668 your¦225672 \add ≈eternal¦225678\add* God¦225672 Yahweh¦225671: May¦225679 \add @the peoples\add* bless¦225679 your¦225681 \add ≈wonderful reputation¦225680\add* which is¦225682 \add ≈greater than anything else that we bless¦225687 or praise¦225688\add*.
\rem /s1 The Prayer of Confession
\v 6 Yahweh¦225693, you¦225694 alone¦225694 are \add @God¦225695\add*. You¦225697 yourself made¦225697 the¦225700 heavens¦225700, the¦225701 \add ≈galaxies in\add* the¦225702 heavens¦225702 and¦225703 all¦225703 their¦225705 \add ≈stars\add*, the¦225706 earth¦225706 and¦225707 all¦225707 that¦225709 is on¦225710 it, the¦225711 seas¦225711 and¦225712 all¦225712 that¦225714 is¦225715 in¦225715 them¦225715. You¦225716 \add ≈give life¦225717 to everything\add*, and \add ≈all the stars bow¦225724 down¦225724\add* to you.
\p
\v 7 “You¦225726 are¦225729 Yahweh¦225729, the¦225730 god who¦225731 chose¦225732 Abram¦225733. Then¦225734 you¦225734 brought¦225734 him¦225734 out¦225734 from¦225735 Ur¦225735 in the¦225736 \add ≈Chaldean region\add*, then¦225737 you¦225737 \add ≈renamed him to\add* Abraham¦225739 \add (meaning ‘father of many’)\add*.
\v 8 You¦225741 \add ≈discovered¦225741 that he was sincere and faithful¦225745 to¦225746 you, and made¦225747 an agreement¦225749 with¦225748 him¦225748\add*—to¦225750 give¦225750 the¦225754 Canaanite¦225754, Hittite, Amorite¦225756, Perizzite, Yebusite¦225758, and¦225759 the¦225759 Girgashite \add ≈regions¦225753\add* to his¦225761 descendants¦225761,\x + \xo 9:8: \xt Gen 15:18-21.\x* and¦225762 you¦225762 have \add ≈ensured that it's all come to be\add* because¦225766 you're righteous¦225767.
\v 9 You \add ≈noticed¦225770 the¦225773 suffering¦225773\add* of¦225773 our¦225774 ancestors¦225774 \add enslaved\add* in¦225775 Egypt¦225775, and¦225776 then you¦225779 heard¦225779 their cry \add for help\add* \add ≈at¦225780 the edge of\add* the Red Sea¦225782.
\p
\v 10 “You \add ≈displayed miracles\add* to Far-oh \add !(Pharaoh)\add*, and to all¦225790 his¦225792 servants¦225792 and¦225793 to all¦225793 the¦225795 \add ≈Egyptian\add* people¦225795, because¦225797 you¦225798 knew¦225798 that¦225799 they¦225800 were acting¦225800 \add ≈as if you weren't real\add*, \add ≈so¦225802 you¦225802 got yourself¦225804 a¦225805 reputation¦225805 which you still have to\add* this¦225807 day¦225806.\x + \xo 9:10: \xt Exo 7:8–12:32.\x*
\v 11 Then¦225809 you¦225810 split¦225810 the sea open¦225810 the sea \add ≈right in¦225811 front¦225811 of¦225811 their eyes\add*, and¦225812 they¦225812 \add ≈walked¦225812\add* through the¦225813 middle¦225813 of¦225813 \add *it\add* on¦225816 dry land¦225816.\x + \xo 9:11: \xt Exo 14:21-29.\x* \add ≈After that,\add* you \add ≈drowned\add* their¦225819 pursuers¦225819 into¦225821 the¦225821 \add ≈deep sea\add* like¦225822 a¦225824 stone¦225824 in¦225825 \add ≈a huge lake\add*.\x + \xo 9:11: \xt Exo 15:4-5.\x*
\v 12 You¦225830 led¦225830 them \add ≈during¦225828 the\add* day¦225831 with a¦225828 pillar¦225828 of¦225828 cloud¦225829, and¦225832 \add ≈during¦225832 the\add* night¦225834 with a¦225832 pillar¦225832 of¦225832 fire¦225833 to¦225835 illuminate¦225835 the¦225839 way¦225839 that¦225840 they¦225841 should go.\x + \xo 9:12: \xt Exo 13:21-22.\x*
\p
